---
import SectionTitleAlt from "@/components/shared/section-title-alt.astro"
---

<section class="flex w-full justify-center overflow-hidden bg-red-50 px-4 xl:rounded-br-4xl xl:rounded-bl-4xl">
  <div class="flex w-full max-w-7xl flex-1 flex-col py-16 lg:py-26">
    <SectionTitleAlt title="About Poster Presentation" subtitle="PREPARATION" />

    <div class="relative grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-[.55fr_1fr] md:gap-10 lg:gap-20">
      <div></div>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-10 leading-8 text-slate-700">
        <div class="space-y-5">
          <p>
            The Poster Presentation is a scientific dissemination session of the 1st HEALTHMED-IC 2026. It provides an opportunity for researchers,
            clinicians, academics, students, and healthcare professionals to communicate research findings in a concise, visual, and accessible
            format.
          </p>

          <p>
            The conference theme is “Innovating Healthcare Excellence: Integrating Advanced Life Treatment and Human- Centered Medicine for a
            Sustainable Future.” Poster submissions should be relevant to the conference scope and demonstrate scientific or practical contributions
            to healthcare and human medicine.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
          <p class="rounded-tl-full rounded-bl-full bg-red-100/50">
            <span class="mr-3 inline-block rounded-full bg-red-900 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-red-50">01</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-red-900">Eligibility and Submission</span>
          </p>

          <ul class="list-outside list-disc space-y-3">
            {
              [
                "Poster presenters must have an accepted abstract or research contribution according to the conference submission and review process.",
                "The submitted work must be original and must not have been simultaneously submitted for publication or presentation in a manner that violates the authors’ institutional or publisher policies.",
                "The content of the poster must be consistent with the submitted abstract. Major changes to the research title, authorship, or scientific content should be communicated to the Organizing Committee.",
                "All authors are responsible for the accuracy, originality, ethical compliance, and appropriate citation of the material presented.",
                "Authors are encouraged to consult the official conference website for the latest submission instructions and deadlines.",
              ].map((item) => <li class="ml-6 pl-2">{item}</li>)
            }
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-8">
          <p class="rounded-tl-full rounded-bl-full bg-red-100/50">
            <span class="mr-3 inline-block rounded-full bg-red-900 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-red-50">02</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-red-900">Recommended Poster Structure</span>
          </p>

          <table>
            <thead class="text-left font-medium text-red-800/70">
              <tr class="bg-red-100/50">
                <th class="p-1 pl-2">Section</th>
                <th class="p-1 pl-2">Recommended Content</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Title</td>
                <td class="p-2">Concise research title reflecting the main topic or finding.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Authors & Affiliations</td>
                <td class="p-2">Full names of all authors, institutional affiliations, country, and corresponding author/contact information.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Background / Introduction</td>
                <td class="p-2">Brief context, research gap, and rationale for the study.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Objective(s)</td>
                <td class="p-2">Clear statement of the main research question, aim, or hypothesis.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Methods</td>
                <td class="p-2">Study design, setting, participants/sample, instruments, procedures, and statistical analysis as appropriate.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Results</td>
                <td class="p-2">Key findings supported by tables, graphs, figures, images, or other relevant visualizations.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Discussion</td>
                <td class="p-2">Brief interpretation of the principal findings and their relevance.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Conclusion</td>
                <td class="p-2">Concise statements directly answering the objective(s).</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Recommendations / Implications</td>
                <td class="p-2">Practical, clinical, public health, educational, technological, or research implications where applicable.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">References</td>
                <td class="p-2">Essential references only, using a consistent academic citation style.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Acknowledgements / Funding / Conflict of Interest</td>
                <td class="p-2">Include where applicable and when relevant to the research.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
          <p class="rounded-tl-full rounded-bl-full bg-red-100/50">
            <span class="mr-3 inline-block rounded-full bg-red-900 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-red-50">03</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-red-900">Poster Specifications</span>
          </p>

          <ul class="list-outside list-disc space-y-3">
            {
              [
                "Recommended size: A0 portrait (84.1 cm × 118.9 cm / 33.1 in × 46.8 in).",
                "Orientation: Portrait. If another size or orientation is required by the conference venue, presenters should follow the latest instruction issued by the Organizing Committee.",
                "File format for submission: PDF (preferred).",
                "Use a clear, professional, high-contrast layout with sufficient white space.",
                "Recommended minimum font sizes: Title 70–90 pt; section headings 32–44 pt; body text 24–32 pt. Adjust as necessary to maintain readability at a distance.",
                "Use high-resolution figures and images. Avoid stretched, pixelated, or excessively compressed visuals.",
                "Graphs and tables should be simple, clearly labeled, and accompanied by appropriate units and legends.",
                "Use consistent typography, alignment, numbering, and citation style throughout the poster.",
                "Avoid excessive text. Prioritize key findings and visual communication.",
                "All figures, photographs, icons, and other third-party materials must be properly attributed or used with appropriate permission/licensing.",
              ].map((item) => <li class="ml-6 pl-2">{item}</li>)
            }
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
          <p class="rounded-tl-full rounded-bl-full bg-red-100/50">
            <span class="mr-3 inline-block rounded-full bg-red-900 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-red-50">04</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-red-900">Research Integrity and Ethical Requirements</span>
          </p>

          <ul class="list-outside list-disc space-y-3">
            {
              [
                "Human and animal research must comply with applicable ethical standards and institutional requirements.",
                "Where applicable, state the ethics approval/clearance information, informed consent status, registration number, or other relevant compliance information.",
                "Do not include identifiable patient information, photographs, or confidential data unless appropriate consent and authorization have been obtained.",
                "Declare funding sources and potential conflicts of interest where applicable.",
                "Plagiarism, fabrication, falsification, duplicate submission, and inappropriate authorship are not permitted.",
              ].map((item, index) => <li class="ml-6 pl-2">{item}</li>)
            }
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
          <p class="rounded-tl-full rounded-bl-full bg-red-100/50">
            <span class="mr-3 inline-block rounded-full bg-red-900 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-red-50">05</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-red-900">Submission Procedure</span>
          </p>

          <ul class="list-outside list-disc space-y-3">
            {
              [
                "Prepare the final poster according to this guideline.",
                "Save the poster as a PDF using the recommended file naming convention: HEALTHMEDIC2026_Poster_[FirstAuthorSurname].pdf",
                "Submit the poster through the designated conference submission system or channel communicated by the Organizing Committee.",
                "Check the final PDF before submission to ensure that fonts, figures, tables, symbols, and special characters display correctly.",
                "Keep a copy of the submitted file for presentation purposes.",
              ].map((item) => <li class="ml-6 pl-2">{item}</li>)
            }
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
          <p class="rounded-tl-full rounded-bl-full bg-red-100/50">
            <span class="mr-3 inline-block rounded-full bg-red-900 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-red-50">06</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-red-900">Poster Presentation</span>
          </p>

          <ul class="list-outside list-disc space-y-3">
            {
              [
                "Presenters should be available during the designated poster presentation session.",
                "The presenting author should be prepared to provide a brief explanation of the study and answer questions from participants, reviewers, or other delegates.",
                "The presentation should emphasize the research problem, methodology, principal findings, and implications.",
                "Presenters should follow the conference schedule and technical instructions provided by the Organizing Committee.",
              ].map((item) => <li class="ml-6 pl-2">{item}</li>)
            }
          </ul>

          <p class="mt-2 ml-6 text-sm">
            For virtual or hybrid presentation arrangements, presenters must follow the specific technical instructions issued by the conference.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
          <p class="rounded-tl-full rounded-bl-full bg-red-100/50">
            <span class="mr-3 inline-block rounded-full bg-red-900 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-red-50">07</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-red-900">Recommended Visual Layout</span>
          </p>

          <p>
            A three-column layout is recommended for portrait posters. A typical flow is: (1) Title and authors, (2) Background and Objective, (3)
            Methods, (4) Results, (5) Discussion, (6) Conclusion/Implications, and (7) References/Acknowledgements. The Results section should receive
            the greatest visual emphasis.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
          <p class="rounded-tl-full rounded-bl-full bg-red-100/50">
            <span class="mr-3 inline-block rounded-full bg-red-900 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-red-50">08</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-red-900">Final Checklist</span>
          </p>

          <ul class="list-outside list-disc space-y-3">
            {
              [
                "Poster follows the recommended A0 portrait format.",
                "Title, authors, affiliations, and corresponding author information are correct.",
                "Abstract content and poster content are consistent.",
                "Objectives and methods are clearly stated.",
                "Main results are easy to identify and supported by appropriate visuals.",
                "Conclusion directly addresses the study objective(s).",
                "References and third-party materials are properly cited.",
                "Ethics, funding, and conflict-of-interest information are included where applicable.",
                "PDF has been checked for readability and technical errors.",
                "File name follows the recommended convention.",
              ].map((item) => <li class="ml-6 pl-2">{item}</li>)
            }
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
          <p class="rounded-tl-full rounded-bl-full bg-red-100/50">
            <span class="mr-3 inline-block rounded-full bg-red-900 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-red-50">09</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-red-900">Final Checklist</span>
          </p>

          <ul class="list-outside list-disc space-y-3">
            {
              [
                "Poster follows the recommended A0 portrait format.",
                "Title, authors, affiliations, and corresponding author information are correct.",
                "Abstract content and poster content are consistent.",
                "Objectives and methods are clearly stated.",
                "Main results are easy to identify and supported by appropriate visuals.",
                "Conclusion directly addresses the study objective(s).",
                "References and third-party materials are properly cited.",
                "Ethics, funding, and conflict-of-interest information are included where applicable.",
                "PDF has been checked for readability and technical errors.",
                "File name follows the recommended convention.",
              ].map((item) => <li class="ml-6 pl-2">{item}</li>)
            }
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-8">
          <p class="rounded-tl-full rounded-bl-full bg-red-100/50">
            <span class="mr-3 inline-block rounded-full bg-red-900 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-red-50">10</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-red-900">Important Dates</span>
          </p>

          <table class="w-full">
            <thead class="text-left font-medium text-red-800/70">
              <tr class="bg-red-100/50">
                <th class="p-1 pl-2">Event</th>
                <th class="p-1 pl-2">Date</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Poster Submission Deadline</td>
                <td class="p-2">October, 15th 2026</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 text-slate-500">Poster Presentation</td>
                <td class="p-2">November, 5th – 7th 2026</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
